  "worked_solution": "First, let's compute the *squared* distance $S(a)$ between the two points. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(a) & ={(3a-4-(-2))}^{2}+{(a+2-6)}^{2} \\\\  & =(3a-2)^{2}+(a-4)^{2} \\\\  & =9{a}^{2}-12a+4+{a}^{2}-8a+16 \\\\  & =10{a}^{2}-20a+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want to minimize $S,$ we compute the derivative ${S}^{\u2032}(a).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{\u2032}(a) & =20a-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe stationary points of $S(a)$ are the points where the derivative ${S}^{\u2032}(a)=0.$ Solving this equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{\u2032}(a) & =0 \\\\ 20a-20 & =0 \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${S}^{\u2033}(1)=20>0.$ Therefore, the squared distance (and therefore the actual distance) reaches a minimum when $b=1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
